# 17. Tuple Immutability

Tuple elements cannot be directly modified.

```python
data = (10, 20, 30)

data[0] = 100
```

This produces:

```text
TypeError
```

---

# 18. Mutable Objects Inside Tuples ⭐

A tuple itself is immutable, but it can contain mutable objects such as lists.

```python
data = (10, [20, 30], 40)

data[1].append(50)

print(data)
# (10, [20, 30, 50], 40)
```

Why is this allowed?

```text
data[0] = 100
→ Not allowed

data[1].append(50)
→ Allowed
```

The tuple cannot change its references, but the **list object stored inside it can change**.

