# 25. List vs Tuple ⭐

| Feature           | List            | Tuple                             |
| ----------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Syntax            | `[ ]`           | `( )`                             |
| Ordered           | Yes             | Yes                               |
| Indexed           | Yes             | Yes                               |
| Iterable          | Yes             | Yes                               |
| Mutable           | ✅ Yes           | ❌ No                              |
| Add elements      | ✅               | ❌                                 |
| Remove elements   | ✅               | ❌                                 |
| Modify elements   | ✅               | ❌                                 |
| Duplicates        | ✅               | ✅                                 |
| Heterogeneous     | ✅               | ✅                                 |
| Nested structures | ✅               | ✅                                 |
| Dynamic size      | ✅               | ❌                                 |
| Memory            | More            | Less                              |
| Performance       | Slightly slower | Generally faster                  |
| Methods           | Many            | Mainly `count()`, `index()`       |
| `sort()`          | Available       | Not available                     |
| `copy()`          | Available       | Not available                     |
| Hashable          | No              | Yes, if all elements are hashable |
| Dictionary key    | ❌               | ✅ If hashable                     |
| Best for          | Changing data   | Fixed data                        |

